<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">True dependency latency for simple INT32/FP32 instructions is ~4 cy=
cles on both Hopper and Blackwell, but throughput is decoupled from latency=
 =E2=80=94 back-to-back <em>independent</em> instructions issue at full rat=
e. So if you have enough independent traversal threads in flight per SM to =
cover the 4-cycle pipeline, you sustain the 128-ops/cycle peak. With your s=
tructure that's easy: each frontier thread carries its own integer state an=
d the next-step ops on different threads have no dependencies between them.=
 <span class=3D"inline-flex" data-state=3D"closed"><a href=3D"https://www.e=
