an></a></span></p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This gets hidden in practice through warp swapping =E2=80=94 while =
one warp waits on its load, the scheduler picks a different warp with opera=
nds ready. The math is tight though: with 64 warps/SM max occupancy =3D 16 =
warps/quadrant and ~30-cycle load latency, each scheduler has 16 warps but =
would need ~30 in flight to fully hide latency on dependent loads. So on a =
pure pointer-chasing workload, each scheduler is idle roughly half the cycl=
es.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Steady-state thread-step throughput for dependent traversal:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
64 warps =C3=97 (1 step / 30 cycles) =E2=89=88 2.1 warp-steps/cycle/SM</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
=C3=97 32 lanes =E2=89=88 68 thread-steps/cycle/SM</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
=C3=97 ~130 SMs =E2=89=88 9000 thread-steps/cycle/chip</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
=C3=97 1.5 GHz =E2=89=88 ~13 trillion thread-steps/sec</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Significantly less than the 128-ops/cycle/SM peak from before =E2=
=80=94 that was the ALU regime; this is the dependent-load regime. Same har=
dware, different bottleneck.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">If your traversal could batch K <em>independent</em> steps per thre=
ad (advance K different starting points sequentially without dependencies a=
mong them), or unroll into K loads issued before the first one returns, you=
'd hide more latency and move toward the ALU-regime throughput. But for gen=
uinely chained pointer-following =E2=80=94 each step's address depends on t=
he previous step's loaded value =E2=80=94 you're load-latency-bound, and th=
e latency budget is what sets the rate.</p></div></div></div></div></div></=
