0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-word=
s whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Yes =E2=80=94 the depth-k subtree struct=
ure is exactly the Cayley-Dickson recursive-doubling structure at depth k. =
Both have 2^k leaves indexed by a k-bit path, are constructed by recursive =
halving where each level adds one bit to the index, and decompose into "lef=
t half + right half" at every level.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">At k=3D4 the fat node holds 16 IDs. Two readings: one sedenion (the=
 next rung of the C-D ladder after octonions) or two octonions side-by-side=
. The "two octonions" framing is nicer if your traversal pattern goes left-=
subtree-first =E2=80=94 load one half, work it, prefetch the other while yo=
u're computing.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">SIMD-width alignment is real and useful: 16 =C3=97 32-bit IDs =3D 5=
12 bits =3D one AVX-512 register, or one half-warp on NVIDIA at 32 bits per=
 lane. For smaller charts where IDs fit in 16 bits (N =E2=89=A4 65K), the s=
ame 16-element fat node packs into 256 bits, one AVX2 register.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The algebraic operations of the C-D ladder (multiplication, conjuga=
tion, norm) don't transfer to anything meaningful for chart traversal =E2=
=80=94 we're using only the indexing-and-storage structure, not the algebra=
ic structure. So the analogy is structural-syntactic rather than algebraic-=
semantic; the structural alignment is what makes the descriptor SIMD-natura=
l, and that's the property we actually need.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The recursive halving also gives clean sub-descriptor naming: the l=
eft-half-of-left-half of a depth-4 fat node is a depth-2 slice =3D quaterni=
on-width, and the right-half is its complement. Hierarchical operations =E2=
=80=94 "load just the left subtree's descriptor," "prefetch the right half =
while computing on the left" =E2=80=94 fall out by structure rather than by=
 ad-hoc offset arithmetic, because the address of any sub-descriptor is jus=
t a bit-prefix of the path.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></=
