p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-=
[1.7]">GF(4) and GF(8) give us proper field structure where GF(2) C-D didn'=
t. In GF(2) C-D, multiplication has zero divisors =E2=80=94 (1,1)=C2=B2 =3D=
 0 at level 1, so it's a ring, not a field. The tower of field extensions G=
F(2) =E2=8A=82 GF(4) =E2=8A=82 GF(16) =E2=8A=82 GF(256) =E2=8A=82 =E2=80=A6=
 is the parallel ladder that gives a field at every rung, with multiplicati=
ve inverses and no zero divisors. Structurally the same recursive-doubling =
shape; algebraically much richer.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The price is that multiplication isn't bitwise =E2=80=94 it's polyn=
omial multiplication modulo an irreducible:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
GF(4) =3D GF(2)[x]/(x=C2=B2+x+1)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
GF(8) =3D GF(2)[x]/(x=C2=B3+x+1)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
GF(2^k) =3D GF(2)[x]/(p(x)) for irreducible p of degree k</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">For small k that's a tiny lookup table; for k=3D8 it's the AES fiel=
d, with hardware support via AES-NI and carry-less-multiply (PCLMULQDQ) ins=
tructions.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Where this could take us:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Polynomial fingerprinting.</strong> Treat a subtree's path-=
pattern as a polynomial over GF(2^k), evaluate at a random point, get a sin=
gle field element as a fingerprint. Collision probability =E2=89=A4 1/2^k. =
Constant-time "are these subtrees structurally equal" probes, useful when h=
ash-consing at large N where bit-by-bit equality scans get slow. The most p=
lausible immediate payoff for chart traversal.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>S-box-style mixing.</strong> AES's S-box is GF(2^8)-inversi=
on plus an affine map =E2=80=94 well-distributed, hardware-supported, one i=
nstruction on modern CPUs. A cheap, high-quality mixer for descriptor hashi=
ng if you want better collision properties than a pure linear fingerprint.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Reed-Solomon-style codes.</strong> If you ever want redunda=
ncy / fault tolerance on the chart (multi-GPU distribution, transient SRAM =
errors at scale), GF(2^k) is the natural setting; corrects up to (2^k - 1)/=
2 erasures per codeword.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Multiplicative inverses for solving.</strong> GF has divisi=
on, so equations like "find x such that A=C2=B7x =3D B" have unique solutio=
ns. Probably not on the traversal hot path but potentially useful for unifi=
cation, pattern matching, or "given this constraint on a subtree, what fill=
s it" queries downstream.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The cleanest framing: the Cayley-Dickson recursion gives you the <e=
m>shape</em> of the descriptor (binary doubling tree of 2^k leaves); the GF=
(2^k) tower tells you what <em>algebra</em> to put on it if you want closed=
-form (field) operations rather than just bitwise (ring) operations. They c=
ompose =E2=80=94 you can use the C-D doubling structure to organize a seque=
nce of GF(2^k)-typed slots, getting both the SIMD-natural layout and field-=
typed operations on the contents.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Which direction sounds load-bearing for your design? Fingerprinting=
 is the lowest-hanging if hash-consing latency starts to matter; the others=
 are speculative until a downstream operation actually needs them.</p></div=
