iv class=3D"standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3=
 standard-markdown"><p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words white=
space-normal leading-[1.7]">Two good points.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Right =E2=80=94 the polynomial-multiplication cost is largely hidde=
n by free cycles in the load-wait regime. If we're spending 30 cycles waiti=
ng on a fetch with only ~5 cycles of dependent ALU work between fetches, th=
e difference between "1 cycle of XOR" and "3 cycles of poly-mul" disappears=
 into the wait. So "bitwise vs polynomial" is a real cost only when we're a=
lready ALU-bound, which we aren't.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">And the precomputation/convolution angle is a clean fit for this st=
ructure specifically. Because the chart is acyclic and incremental (rule k =
depends only on rules &lt; k), any function f over the chart can be propaga=
ted incrementally: at insertion, f(k) =3D combine(f(l), f(q)) where (l, q) =
are k's children. O(1) work per insert, valid forever afterward.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Three concrete things this buys:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Subtree fingerprints.</strong> Every rule stores a precompu=
ted fingerprint of its full subtree, computed at insertion as fingerprint(k=
) =3D mix(fingerprint(l), fingerprint(q)). Subtree-equality becomes a singl=
e field-element comparison =E2=80=94 O(1) instead of O(subtree size). The m=
ix can be a GF(2^k) poly step or one S-box round.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Pre-mixed descriptors.</strong> The fat-node descriptor at =
insertion can be stored already in its target representation =E2=80=94 alre=
ady permuted, XORed against a mask, S-box transformed. Every traversal load=
 returns clean, pre-mixed data; the per-step mix moves from query time to i=
nsert time.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>LUT-applied edges.</strong> Each (left, right) edge stored =
as a pre-looked-up value rather than the raw ID =E2=80=94 the AES-S-box ima=
