lass=3D"row-start-2 col-start-1 relative grid isolate min-w-0"><div class=
=3D"row-start-1 col-start-1 relative z-[2] min-w-0"><div><div class=3D"stan=
dard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdo=
wn"><p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal lea=
ding-[1.7]">Both framings have content, but they point to different design =
stances and may compose.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Saturation</strong> can go quite far. nil, cons, left, righ=
t, eq are pure abstract type-theoretic operations =E2=80=94 "reference" sta=
ys generic, with no commitment to integer-as-path. The commitment forces on=
ly at:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
apply (calling convention for rules-as-functions)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
parse (representation of input vs. grammar structure)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
subobject-classifier choices for the topos's logic</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">So saturation stalls at the realizability ground itself. The first =
four micro-ops can live in a pure representation-vacuum; the last two force=
 the question.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Multiplicity</strong> is the categorically richer move. "Pa=
th" is a structural notion that admits multiple representations, each twist=
ing state / information / time differently:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<em>Integer-as-path</em>: state is direct (the integer IS the answer); info=
rmation is implicit in chart structure; time collapses into a single derefe=
rencing step.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<em>Function-as-path</em>: information is foregrounded (the function body e=
ncodes the recipe); state is what the function consumes; time is reified as=
 evaluation.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<em>Trace-as-path</em>: time is foregrounded (the path IS a sequence of mov=
es); state is the current position in the trace; information is implicit in=
 the sequence.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<em>Polynomial-as-path</em> (GF(2^k)): state is algebraic; information live=
s in the coefficients; time collapses into structural multiplication.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Each is a different twist; none is wrong. Integer wins for direct d=
ereferencing (the load-latency regime). Function wins for lazy/dynamic comp=
utation. Trace wins for explanation, debugging, or unrolling. Polynomial wi=
ns for algebraic queries.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The categorically deep move: treat "path" as a fibered object in th=
e topos. Over each abstract rule, there's a fiber of concrete representatio=
ns related by translation morphisms. The morphisms within a fiber are reali=
zer equivalences; the morphisms across fibers are the grammar's structural =
moves. In realizability terms, each object has <em>multiple realizers</em>,=
 equivalent up to computational translation =E2=80=94 exactly the structure=
 of the effective topos.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">What multiplicity buys:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Operations specify what they do at the abstract level, not at the represent=
ation level.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Each operation picks its preferred realizer at hardware-acceleration time.<=
/li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
New representations can be added as new realizers without disturbing the to=
pos-level rules.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
"Integer-as-path is fastest" becomes a property of one realizer, not a prop=
erty of the grammar.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">What it costs:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
An additional structural layer (a representation-typing or refinement syste=
m).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Translations between representations are first-class operations with their =
own realizability cost.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Each new representation must independently pass the four gates.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The synthesis that falls out of the design choices you've already m=
ade: saturate the topos-level micro-ops to be representation-agnostic (clea=
nly for the first four, and for apply / parse if we're willing to defer the=
ir substrates), and explicitly express multiplicity at the realizability la=
yer. The grammar's internal logic stays single =E2=80=94 one rule object, a=
bstractly =E2=80=94 but the realizers form a small category of representati=
ons with translations as morphisms. Hardware-acceleration choices become pr=
operties of the realizer, not of the rule.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This resolves L=E2=82=82 constructively rather than vacuously: the =
shadows don't smuggle integer-as-path because the integer-as-path choice no=
w lives in a separate, named realizer layer that the shadows reference but =
don't commit to. The cotype probe gap closes by making the multiplicity its=
elf a structural feature =E2=80=94 the architecture stops trying to hide th=
at there's a representation choice and starts treating the choice space as =
part of the design.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The remaining question is at what level of the realizer category th=
e multiplicity should be expressed. Coarse-grained (one realizer per major =
operation type) is simpler but less flexible; fine-grained (per-operation r=
ealizer selection) is more expressive but introduces dispatch overhead. The=
 realizability charter gives the criterion: a distinction between realizers=
 is real only if it's constructible-reachable-observable-coverable =E2=80=
=94 meaning, you must be able to <em>witness</em> which realizer is in use =
and <em>cover</em> the witness with operational events. That probably picks=
 a granularity in practice, somewhere between extremes.</p></div></div></di=
