_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class=3D"font-claude-response-=
body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Modeling the five as a CS=
P makes the dominant forces visible. Each open question is a variable; the =
constraints fall into five force categories:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>A =E2=80=94 Topos/semantic</strong>: CCC totality, =CE=A9 structure=
, morphism composability.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>B =E2=80=94 Charter</strong>: constructible/reachable/observable/co=
verable.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>C =E2=80=94 Operational</strong>: efficiency, hardware-acceleration=
 friendliness, dispatch cost.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>D =E2=80=94 Compositional</strong>: how the choice composes with do=
wnstream operations.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>E =E2=80=94 Self-extending</strong>: meta-circular and bootstrap re=
quirements.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">For each variable, the forces accumulate and the dominant force det=
ermines the resolution.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">C1 =E2=80=
=94 <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-d=
anger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">le=
ft(nil)</code> / <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bord=
er-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text=
-[0.9rem]">right(nil)</code>: defined or undefined?</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Domain: { defined-as-nil, defined-as-failure, undefined }.</p>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6"><table class=3D"min-w-full =
border-collapse text-sm leading-[1.7] whitespace-normal"><thead class=3D"te=
xt-left"><tr><th scope=3D"col" class=3D"text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-b=
order-300/60 py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Force</th><th scope=3D"col" cla=
ss=3D"text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-border-300/60 py-2 pr-4 align-top f=
ont-bold">Direction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 b=
order-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">A: CCC requires total morphisms</t=
d><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">defin=
ed</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 al=
ign-top">B: failure must be observable + coverable</td><td class=3D"border-=
b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">defined-as-something</td></=
tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">=
C: no exception machinery needed</td><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-borde=
r-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">defined</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.=
5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">D: composes uniformly with eq, =
cons</td><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top=
">defined</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 =
pr-4 align-top">E: meta-rules traverse arbitrary structures without crashin=
g</td><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">d=
efined</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Resolution: <strong>defined as nil</strong>. nil is the absorbing e=
lement of projections. Discrimination is recovered via <code class=3D"bg-te=
xt-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre=
-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">eq(left(k), nil)</code> =
=E2=80=94 O(1) check. The undefined option costs exception machinery that h=
as no compensating semantic gain.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">C2 =E2=80=
=94 Designated rule identities</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Domain: any assignment of small indices to nil, true, false, failur=
e.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Forces: A says =CE=A9 needs exactly two distinct elements (true =E2=
=89=A0 false). B says distinct concepts get distinct identities. C says sma=
llest indices (cheap dispatch, fewer bits). D says consistent with hash-con=
sing =E2=80=94 once chosen, identities are canonical.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Resolution:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">nil</c=
ode> =3D 0 =E2=80=94 term-algebra base</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">true</=
code> =3D cons(nil, nil) =3D 1 =E2=80=94 smallest non-nil, first element of=
 =CE=A9</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">false<=
/code> =3D cons(nil, cons(nil, nil)) =3D 2 =E2=80=94 distinct from nil, sec=
ond element of =CE=A9</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">failur=
e</code> =3D cons(cons(nil, nil), nil) =3D 3 =E2=80=94 distinct from all of=
 the above</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Allocated at chart initialization; subsequent rules from S2 occupy =
indices =E2=89=A5 4. The alternative of collapsing nil/false/failure into a=
 single absorbing element saves identities but loses semantic distinctions =
that downstream operations will want to make.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">C3 =E2=80=
=94 <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-d=
anger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">ap=
ply</code> evaluation strategy</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Domain: { CBV, CBN, CBNeed }.</p>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6"><table class=3D"min-w-full =
border-collapse text-sm leading-[1.7] whitespace-normal"><thead class=3D"te=
xt-left"><tr><th scope=3D"col" class=3D"text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-b=
order-300/60 py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold">Force</th><th scope=3D"col" cla=
ss=3D"text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-border-300/60 py-2 pr-4 align-top f=
ont-bold">Direction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 b=
order-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">A: CCC equations hold under any st=
rategy</td><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-t=
op">neutral</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-=
2 pr-4 align-top">B: charter wants observable, deterministic ops</td><td cl=
ass=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">any determini=
stic</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 =
align-top">C: efficiency on terminating computations</td><td class=3D"borde=
r-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">CBNeed &gt; CBV &gt; CBN<=
/td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align=
-top">D: hash-consing is memoization at data level</td><td class=3D"border-=
b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">CBNeed (computation memoiza=
tion aligns)</td></tr><tr><td class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py=
-2 pr-4 align-top">E: self-referential / infinite grammar structures</td><t=
d class=3D"border-b-0.5 border-border-300/30 py-2 pr-4 align-top">CBN or CB=
Need (CBV loops forever)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Resolution: <strong>call-by-need</strong>. C+D+E align; A is neutra=
l. Each computation result becomes a new rule, hash-consed; identical compu=
tations always produce the same result-rule, so memoization is structural r=
ather than imposed.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">C4 =E2=80=
=94 <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-d=
anger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">pa=
rse</code> grammar argument</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Domain: { implicit, explicit, hybrid-with-default }.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Forces: A says explicit is more functorial. C says implicit is more=
 convenient at call sites. D and E both force explicit =E2=80=94 meta-gramm=
ar parsing object-grammar text requires <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border=
 border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[=
0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">parse(meta_grammar, grammar_text)</code>,=
 and that argument can't be the live grammar (since the live grammar IS the=
 meta-grammar in that case).</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Resolution: <strong>explicit</strong>. D+E dominate. Convenience fo=
r the common case is recovered as a derived rule: <code class=3D"bg-text-20=
0/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap=
 rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">parse_live(input) =3D parse(liv=
e_grammar_ref, input)</code>, where <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bor=
der-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4r=
em] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">live_grammar_ref</code> is itself a rule.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">C5 =E2=80=
=94 Failure encoding</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Domain: { designated-rule, exception, sum-type }.</p>
