<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Cross-vari=
able constraints</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The variables are not independent. The interactions form a coherent=
 web:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>C1 =E2=88=A7 C5</strong>: nil and failure are distinct values; nil =
represents "no further structure," failure represents "exceptional outcome.=
" Both are designated rules (per C2), so the system can discriminate them i=
n O(1).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>C2 =E2=88=A7 C5</strong>: the failure value is one of the designate=
d rules, occupying index 3. Initialization reserves four indices total.</li=
>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>C3 =E2=88=A7 chart-monotonicity</strong>: CBNeed's memoization work=
s because the chart never invalidates =E2=80=94 computed result-rules persi=
st forever, just like input rules.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>C3 =E2=88=A7 C5</strong>: <em>non-termination is NOT covered by the=
 designated failure rule</em>. This is the load-bearing residual tension =
=E2=80=94 see below.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>C4 =E2=88=A7 E</strong>: explicit grammar is what makes the meta-ci=
rcular fixpoint expressible. Implicit would collapse the meta/object distin=
ction at the wrong layer.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Residual t=
ensions</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The biggest residual force-imbalance: <strong>non-termination of ap=
ply</strong> is not a "failure" in the C5 sense and cannot be made one with=
out changing the system's nature.</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
CBNeed can compute forever (Turing-completeness implies undecidable termina=
tion).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Detection of non-termination is not constructible in general (this is exact=
ly what G=C3=B6del ate).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The realizability charter's "coverable" gate is satisfied because the <em>d=
istinction</em> between terminating-and-failing vs. non-terminating is not =
a runtime distinction the system needs to make =E2=80=94 non-termination is=
 an absence of any outcome, not a specific outcome the system observes.</li=
>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Resolution: accept it. Non-termination is intrinsic to a Turing-com=
plete realizability ground. The system can optionally support a fueled vari=
ant <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-d=
anger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">ap=
ply_fueled(f, x, budget) =E2=86=92 result | failure</code> as an additional=
 micro-op (not founding), which makes bounded computation observable. The f=
ounding <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 te=
xt-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]=
">apply</code> is unbounded and may not terminate.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This residual tension is the deepest entailment of the system's des=
ign: it's the operational shadow of G=C3=B6del's theorem at the realizabili=
ty layer. The charter accepts it because it's not a <em>runtime distinction=
</em> the system tries and fails to make; it's an <em>unavoidable property<=
/em> of the substrate.</p>
