se-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The realizability char=
ter now holds at every layer: every distinction the <em>system</em> makes i=
s constructible/reachable/observable/coverable. Non-termination is no longe=
r "a property the system has"; it's "a property certain programs we write h=
ave." That's a much more principled framing =E2=80=94 the substrate is well=
-behaved, and programs are responsible for their own termination behavior.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This also explains why a compiler is even possible for Turing-compl=
ete languages: the compiler operates entirely in apply-as-step territory, n=
ever trying to evaluate fully. It can do arbitrarily sophisticated transfor=
mations because each transformation is bounded. The compiler is itself a fi=
xed-point of apply-as-step transformations applied to itself =E2=80=94 whic=
h terminates because the transformations are structural, even though the co=
mpiled programs may not.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div=
