<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Monomial multiplication x^a =C2=B7 y^b =C2=B7 z^c (G=C3=B6del-like, lives i=
n the free abelian monoid on indeterminates).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Substitution f(g, h, =E2=80=A6) (de Bruijn-like, replacing variables in pol=
ynomials with other polynomials).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
These interact via the distributive law: (ab) =E2=88=98 =CF=83 =3D (a =E2=
=88=98 =CF=83)(b =E2=88=98 =CF=83).</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Categorically, this is the <strong>free symmetric operad</strong> o=
n a signature. Operads encode operations-with-arities under composition; th=
e symmetric version adds commutativity at the argument level. Both G=C3=B6d=
el-style sequencing and de Bruijn-style substitution are first-class operad=
ic operations.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Magma comp=
osition</h3>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
G=C3=B6del decomposes into (=E2=84=95, =C2=B7) =3D free abelian monoid on c=
ountably many primes.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
de Bruijn decomposes into the free operad on the lambda signature.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The free symmetric operad on a signature is the composed structure that adm=
its both =E2=80=94 sequencing comes from the abelian-monoid layer, substitu=
tion from the operadic-composition layer, and their interaction is governed=
