<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>HOTRS</strong>: named variables, =CE=B1-equivalence (most explicit =
grade).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>de Bruijn</strong>: nameless indices (middle grade).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Combinators</strong>: no variables (most abstracted grade).</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The compilers form a composition: HOTRS =E2=86=92 de Bruijn =E2=86=
=92 combinators. The coherence =E2=80=94 that the composite HOTRS =E2=86=92=
 combinators equals the sequential HOTRS =E2=86=92 de Bruijn =E2=86=92 comb=
inators up to canonical equivalence =E2=80=94 is the associativity of compi=
ler composition. Stasheff's tower of associahedra K_n governs these coheren=
ces at each arity of composition.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This is a <strong>second associahedron</strong> in the design =E2=
=80=94 M2's was over representations. Both share the categorical home from =
M6: the free symmetric operad in a topos, where every level of composition =
is governed by appropriate Stasheff coherences.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Implications:</p>
<ol class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex=
-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The choice of "founding" formal system is a <strong>vertex selection</stron=
g>. Any vertex works; we picked combinators because it fits the chart. Rota=
tions to other vertices are admissible and coherent.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Hardware acceleration could target any vertex. Combinators-on-hardware is o=
ne option; de Bruijn-on-hardware another; HOTRS-on-hardware the most ambiti=
ous. Each is a valid choice with coherent rotations.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The compiler API =E2=86=92 storage is an edge of this associahedron. Cohere=
nce with other compilation paths guarantees the architecture isn't lock-in.=
</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The deeper pattern: every design choice in this architecture has an=
 associahedron structure. M2 over representations. M7 over formal systems. =
The architecture is a <strong>tower of associahedra</strong>, each level go=
verning coherence of one kind of choice. The transform micro-op (S7) is the=
 realization of rotations at both levels =E2=80=94 it's the operadic rotati=
on operation, polymorphic over what kind of rotation. The associahedra are =
level-specific; the rotation operation is general.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Once the pattern is recognized, every design choice can be asked: "=
what's the associahedron here?" The polytope of options with canonical rota=
tions and Stasheff coherences is the answer. This is what makes the grade-s=
panning a structural move rather than a one-off convenience.</p>
