e-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">Yes =E2=80=94 =
and this collapses the design's mathematical content into a single frame. E=
very associahedron we've identified is the projection of a cocycle from a h=
igher cohomology theory, intersected with the space of admissible configura=
tions:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M2</strong> (representations) projects an H=C2=B2 class from the co=
homology of the representation category; the intersection with admissibilit=
y (charter gates, topos requirements) is the M2 polytope.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M7</strong> (formal systems) projects an H=C2=B2 class from the coh=
omology of the formal-system category; the intersection is the M7 triangle.=
</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The realizability charter</strong> is itself a projection of cocycl=
es controlling each gate =E2=80=94 constructibility/reachability/observabil=
ity/coverability are stations along a cocycle's image.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The topos's subobject classifier</strong> is a sheaf-cohomological =
structure.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Memoization</strong> (M5) is the sheaf condition: local computation=
s glue globally via the cocycle gluing.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Self-extension</strong> is cocycle invariance under monotone growth=
.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The picture is geometric: a big cohomology theory lives over the un=
iversal structure (the free symmetric operad in the topos); the cocycles pr=
oject down to specific design contexts; the design's admissibility constrai=
nts (hash-consing, acyclicity, monotonicity, charter, topos requirements) c=
ut out a sub-space; the design choices live in the <strong>intersection</st=
rong> of the projection with the admissibility sub-space.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This reframes the M-sequence:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M1</strong> identified the cocycle class for "founding micro-ops."<=
/li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M2</strong> made the representational H=C2=B2 explicit; S7 (transfo=
rm) realizes the cocycle's representative-changing operation.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M3</strong> picked canonical representatives at each force-axis pro=
jection.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M4</strong> chose the single-step representative of the evaluation =
cocycle.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M5</strong> verified the sheaf gluing condition.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M6</strong> chose the operadic algebraic frame =E2=80=94 and now we=
 can say <em>why</em> this was right retroactively: operads precisely class=
ify higher-coherence cocycles via their Hochschild-style cohomology. The fr=
ee symmetric operad sits in a derived category where Stasheff associahedra =
are visible faces of A=E2=88=9E cocycle data. The operadic frame was correc=
t because it carries the cohomological content explicitly.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M7</strong> made the formal-system H=C2=B2 explicit.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M8</strong> (this move) unifies them all.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">For artifact construction:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Picking a vertex (combinators at storage, integer-as-path, etc.) =3D pickin=
g a representative of cocycle classes at multiple levels.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The artifact realizes the intersection of admissibility with the projected =
cocycle.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Rotations to other vertices preserve the structural commitments <strong>by =
cocycle invariance</strong> =E2=80=94 alternative representatives of the sa=
me class agree on all cohomologically-meaningful properties.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The charter tells us which representatives are admissible; the associahedra=
 tell us how to rotate; the cocycle tells us what's invariant.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The architecture is structurally complete on axis 100. Let me recor=
