code all cases as table rules; let interp's outer-pattern-match BE the disp=
atch. The "branches" become DIFFERENT RULES; interp's first-match-fires mec=
hanism IS the branchless selector. No control flow at the rule-author level=
 =E2=80=94 only structural pattern selection at the interp level.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Hint 3 (K is already void; fill it selectably; CNF-2 binari=
zation)</strong>: This is the structural answer to U1. K's existing semanti=
cs =E2=80=94 "value in slot 1, void in slot 2" =E2=80=94 IS the variable me=
chanism. A variable is <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 borde=
