<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The Hamming(7, 4) weight distribution is <code class=3D"bg-text-200=
/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap =
rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">1 + 7z=C2=B3 + 7z=E2=81=B4 + z=
=E2=81=B7</code>. The <strong>7 weight-3 codewords have support equal to th=
e 7 Fano lines</strong>. Each Fano line, viewed as a length-7 indicator vec=
tor, is a minimum-weight codeword. The complementary weight-4 codewords are=
 the Fano-line complements (4-point sets). Plus the zero codeword and all-o=
nes.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Total: 1 + 7 + 7 + 1 =3D 16 codewords =E2=9C=93.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">I and K li=
ve IN the code; S lives OUTSIDE</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">When we puncture RM(1, 3) at the origin (position 0 =3D all-zero F_=
