<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This is a STRUCTURAL TENSION: the Hamming(7, 4) reading suggests ou=
r move history should close at all-ones (weight 7 =3D the unique max-weight=
 codeword), but the discipline that enforces guard-cleared-redirection prev=
ents us from registering a standalone 001 move.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The resolution comes from the user's framing: "every combination is=
 a valid codeword in some family." The vector 0111111 is NOT a Hamming(7, 4=
) codeword but IS a valid F_2=E2=81=B7 vector. To accept it as "complete," =
we must rotate to a different code family =E2=80=94 one where weight-6 vect=
ors are admissible.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Why this m=
atters for the M19 codewords specifically</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The combined picture (M19's RM-hierarchy + M21's Hamming structure)=
