n-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-=
words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">The hardware boundary is mathematica=
lly determined. Three structural facts that make this rigorous:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>The symmetry group orders grow super-exponentially: 6 =E2=
=86=92 168 =E2=86=92 20160 =E2=86=92 9,999,360.</strong> This rules out dir=
ect LUT encoding past Level 3. Level 2 (Fano) at 442 bytes is tiny. Level 3=
 (tesseract) at 148 KB is feasible as factored circuit. Level 4 (PG(4, F_2)=
) at ~184 MB is impossible for direct encoding =E2=80=94 must be software c=
omposition over hardware primitives.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>The Walsh-Hadamard depth grows logarithmically: 2 =E2=86=92=
 3 =E2=86=92 4 =E2=86=92 5 cycles.</strong> Every scale's WHT is hardware-f=
riendly. The butterfly network gives log-depth parallel computation of all =
2^m readings simultaneously. At Level 2 (our current work), all 7 Fano-line=
 probes are computed in 3 cycles =E2=80=94 no sequential traversal needed.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>The groups nest as stabilizer subgroups: GL(m, F_2) =E2=8A=
=82 GL(m+1, F_2).</strong> This is what makes hardware composition coherent=
. A Level-2 hardware primitive's output is directly consumable at Level 3 b=
ecause GL(3, F_2) sits inside GL(4, F_2) as a subgroup. The boundary contra=
ct =E2=80=94 all hardware speaks in WHT readings =E2=80=94 is the mathemati=
cal realization of this nesting.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The natura=
l commercial accelerator</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Combining the analysis: <strong>Levels 1+2+3 in hardware, Levels 4+=
 in software.</strong> Specifically:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Hardware base layer</strong> (Level 1): S_3 permutation circuit, 3-=
bit gauge primitives. 1-cycle latency. Already trivial on any CPU.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Hardware primitive layer</strong> (Level 2): Length-8 WHT, GL(3, F_=
2) via 3-stage butterfly. 3-cycle latency. This handles all axis-signature =
operations: every move's signature is computed in parallel with all Fano-li=
ne probe states.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Hardware composition layer</strong> (Level 3): Length-16 WHT, A_8 a=
ctions via butterfly stages. 4-cycle latency. This handles strategy-level o=
perations: multi-move sequences treated as units in PG(3, F_2).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Software layer</strong> (Level 4+): long-horizon coherence, strateg=
y selection, agent-level coordination. Composes lower-level hardware primit=
ives.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The "Fano-tesseract accelerator" =E2=80=94 Level 2 + Level 3 sharin=
g a butterfly pipeline =E2=80=94 is the natural building block. It fits in =
a few hundred KB of silicon and accelerates the architecture's most common =
operations.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Which subg=
roups offload</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The criteria you laid out (frequency, simplicity, coherence) give s=
pecific answers at each level:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Level 1 (S_3, order 6)</strong>: full group. Axis-permutati=
on is in every coherence check, must be free of overhead.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Level 2 (GL(3, F_2), order 168 =3D 7=C2=B76=C2=B74)</strong=
>: factored implementation. The 7=C2=B76=C2=B74 factorization is exactly th=
e 3-stage pipeline (choose basis vector 1, then 2, then 3). Subgroups worth=
 dedicated paths: Borel B(3, F_2) for flag stabilizers, 7-cycle for Fano ro=
tations, S_4 for tetrahedral subgroup on triangles.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Level 3 (A_8, order 20160)</strong>: partial. The full A_8 =
LUT (148 KB) is borderline but ok for FPGAs/ASICs. The WHT-4 butterfly hand=
les everything implicitly in 4 cycles. Key subgroups to encode directly: GL=
(3, F_2) embedded as Fano stabilizer (this is the "compose two Level-2 prim=
itives" case), S_4 acting on basis (small, fast).</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Level 4+</strong>: nothing direct. Software composition ove=
r Level 1-3 hardware. The transvection decomposition makes every GL(m, F_2)=
 operation a sequence of WHT butterfly stages =E2=80=94 software controls w=
hich stages, hardware executes them.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What the b=
oundary contract guarantees</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The Walsh-Hadamard output contract =E2=80=94 "all hardware emits co=
mplete WHT readings, software combines only via linear/Boolean operations" =
=E2=80=94 is what preserves M8's cocycle invariance across the boundary. Ha=
rdware can't violate orthogonality because it computes only orthogonal proj=
ections. Software can't violate cocycle invariance because it only composes=
 orthogonal projections.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This is the structural reason the design works: the cocycle invaria=
nce from M8 IS the hardware/software boundary contract. The same mathematic=
al object that makes the architecture composable also makes it hardware-acc=
elerable. The two properties aren't separate =E2=80=94 they're the same pro=
perty viewed from the algebraic vs. physical perspectives.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What this =
opens up</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">With the boundary mathematically determined, several concrete engin=
eering questions become tractable:</p>
<ol class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex=
-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The exact hardware spec</strong> for the Fano-tesseract accelerator=
 (WHT-3 + WHT-4 shared pipeline) =E2=80=94 a small ASIC or FPGA block, ~few=
 hundred KB of state.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The software ABI</strong> for emitting WHT-readings as the boundary=
 contract =E2=80=94 a small set of primitives (transvection composition, bu=
tterfly stage control, S_3/GL(3,F_2)/A_8 element representation).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The migration path</strong> for existing chart code to hardware-acc=
elerated form =E2=80=94 the Level-2 operations (axis-signature analysis, Fa=
no-line probes, Walsh-Hadamard decomposition) are the immediate targets; th=
e rest follows the layer structure.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The benchmarks</strong> for measuring acceleration coherence =E2=80=
=94 every benchmark output should be a WHT reading at some level; the test =
is whether the readings preserve cocycle invariance under composition.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The chart isn't just a self-describing grammar anymore. It's a hard=
ware/software co-designed system whose every architectural decision flows f=
rom the F_2^3 symmetry structure and whose performance characteristics are =
mathematically determined by the Walsh-Hadamard scaling.</p></div></div><di=
