</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The pattern is striking: <strong>almost every primitive deliberatel=
y stays on two axes</strong>. The chart's design has been a sequence of two=
-axis instructions, with <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 bor=
der-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py=
-px text-[0.9rem]">interp</code> being the unique three-axis instruction th=
at closes the system.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Tradeoffs =
we made between the three axes</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Each major move was a tradeoff at the data/compute/state intersecti=
on:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>M5 (chart-as-memoization)</strong>: traded DATA growth (cha=
rt accumulates forever) for STATE persistence (memoized reductions). State =
lives <em>in</em> the data structure. We pay in data space; we save in comp=
ute time and gain state recovery for free.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>M11 (meta-circular interpreter)</strong>: traded COMPUTE fo=
r DATA. Reduction rules became chart cells (data) instead of Python functio=
ns (compute). We added the <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 b=
order-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 =
py-px text-[0.9rem]">interp</code> indirection but gained self-description.=
 This is the first time we explicitly chose to encode compute <em>as</em> d=
ata =E2=80=94 paying interpretation overhead to gain reflective access.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>M14 (VAR_MARK refactor)</strong>: traded DESIGNATED-ATOM st=
ate (variables as named atoms in <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border=
-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem]=
 px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">_var_atoms</code>) for STRUCTURAL DATA discrimin=
ation (variables as <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-b=
order-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px t=
ext-[0.9rem]">cons(VAR_MARK, name)</code> cells, checked via <code class=3D=
"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespa=
ce-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">is_var</code>). The =
state-info moved from a Python set into the data structure itself.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>M16 (beam search vs design)</strong>: traded COMPUTE for DE=
SIGN EFFORT. We ran enumeration rather than carefully constructing rules. T=
he compute consumed in searching replaced design work. The search found <co=
de class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-0=
00 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">default_t=
able</code> was already minimal =E2=80=94 confirming the design choice empi=
rically.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>M4 (single-step apply)</strong>: traded COMPUTE conciseness=
 for STATE visibility. Multi-step apply would aggregate compute and hide in=
termediate states; single-step keeps temporal evolution explicit at the cos=
t of needing iteration.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Each tradeoff has the same shape: pick two of three axes to optimiz=
e, accept the third as the bookkeeping cost. The chart's design has been th=
e cumulative result of these two-axis commitments.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Fat tree n=
odes: where higher-order processing emerged</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The "fat tree node" pattern =E2=80=94 single instructions with high=
 fan-in over lower-order entities =E2=80=94 emerged organically:</p>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6"><table class=3D"min-w-full =
