nt-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">You're=
 right =E2=80=94 the SPPF transcript has the actual axis decomposition I wa=
s missing. Reading back through it, the entire data structure design walked=
 the data/compute/state axes systematically. Let me map what was already th=
ere.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The SPPF d=
esign moves, mapped to the three axes</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>DATA + STATE moves (storage layout that carries temporal ev=
olution):</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-d=
anger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">(R=
, 2, N)</code> bitmask stack =E2=80=94 every rule is a 2=C3=97N array; rule=
 index =3D position in the stack =3D insertion time. Data structure literal=
ly IS the state evolution.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Trailing-zeros equivalence =E2=80=94 "a rule added at N=3D10 with bits B is=
 the same rule as one added at N=3D20 with B=E2=80=960..0" =E2=80=94 state-=
progress-invariant identity.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Hash-consing across N-epochs =E2=80=94 strip-then-hash makes idempotent-add=
s idempotent across state advances.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Acyclicity by construction =E2=80=94 rule k references only rules &lt;k. St=
ate ordering constrains data references.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Monotonic chart growth =E2=80=94 every state advance creates new data, neve=
r retracts.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Insertion order =3D rule index =E2=80=94 the freest binding of data identit=
y to state position.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Subtree fingerprints precomputed at insert =E2=80=94 <code class=3D"bg-text=
-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-w=
rap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">fingerprint(k) =3D mix(finge=
rprint(l), fingerprint(q))</code> =E2=80=94 state advance produces derived =
data that's then fixed forever.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>DATA + COMPUTE moves (representation choices that change co=
mpute affordances):</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
One-hot vs integer encoding =E2=80=94 same data, different compute. One-hot=
: <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dan=
ger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">2R</=
code> bits, dense scan vectorizes. Integer: <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 bo=
rder border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap round=
ed-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">2log=E2=82=82R</code> bits, gather/sc=
atter required. Same content, dual compute regimes.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Dense <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text=
-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">=
(R, 2, N)</code> vs adjacency list =E2=80=94 same content, dense lets <code=
 class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000=
 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">np.all(arr[=
:, 0] =3D=3D B1, axis=3D1)</code> vectorize across the chart in one filter;=
 adjacency list trades the filter away.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
BWT vs raw bits =E2=80=94 same content, compute moves from bitwise AND/OR i=
nto rank/select land.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
GF(2) vs GF(2^k) algebra =E2=80=94 same bit substrate, different algebraic =
compute (rings with zero divisors vs proper fields with inverses).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Morton/heap-relative layout =E2=80=94 data layout enabling integer-arithmet=
ic compute. <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-30=
0 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9=
rem]">parent =3D (i-1) &gt;&gt; 1</code>, LCA via <code class=3D"bg-text-20=
0/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap=
 rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">i XOR j</code> and <code class=
=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 white=
space-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">clz</code>. Addre=
ss arithmetic IS the compute.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
AES S-box / LUT-applied edges =E2=80=94 pre-applied transformation folds th=
e compute into the data.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>COMPUTE + STATE moves (algorithm design that advances state=
 via compute):</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The =CE=B6 insertion operator =E2=80=94 content-blind position permutation =
+ zero injection + new bit placement. Compute that mechanically advances th=
e chart state.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Dynamic BWT update via LF-mapping =E2=80=94 compute path through state, O(p=
olylog R) per inserted bit.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The witness-application principle =E2=80=94 =CE=A6_R describes the many-to-=
many abstract relation; AND with the in-hand state <code class=3D"bg-text-2=
00/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wra=
p rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">(B, =CF=81)</code> collapses i=
t to the singleton <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bo=
rder-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px te=
xt-[0.9rem]">B'</code>. <strong>State (the held witness) narrows compute (t=
he abstract relation).</strong></li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Fat-node depth-k ancestor propagation =E2=80=94 at insert, k state-update c=
ompute steps propagate new descendants upward. Trades insert-time compute f=
or query-time clarity.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
Frontier advancement =E2=80=94 SIMT compute step that changes per-thread st=
ate while reusing shared data.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>The unique triadic moves (all three engaged):</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
The full insertion pipeline <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 =
border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1=
 py-px text-[0.9rem]">=CE=B6 =E2=88=98 hash-cons =E2=88=98 position-assign<=
/code> =E2=80=94 creates data (new bits) via compute (=CE=B6 permutation) a=
t new state (incremented R). The chart's primitive constructor is triadic.<=
/li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
BWT-as-operational-form with FM-index =E2=80=94 the regime where state-awar=
e compressed compute operates on persistent data. The decision to keep BWT =
as operational rather than cold storage was the choice to live in the triad=
ic mode.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The fat tr=
ee nodes we explicitly built</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Reading back, every fat structure was identified precisely as an ag=
gregator trading insertion cost for query-time clarity:</p>
<ol class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex=
-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-30=
0 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9=
rem]">(R, 2, N)</code> chart itself</strong> =E2=80=94 one fat structure co=
ntaining every rule's bitmasks, enabling broadcast equality compare.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The depth-4 fat node descriptor</strong> =E2=80=94 16 IDs per node =
(2 octonions / 1 sedenion), 512 bits =3D one AVX-512 register / one half-wa=
rp. Trades ancestor-update at insert for <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 borde=
r border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-=
[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">1/k + 1</code> instructions per query st=
ep. Recursive doubling structure exactly matches Cayley-Dickson.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>The BWT'd chart with rank/select auxiliaries</strong> =E2=80=94 sin=
gle compressed structure providing O(log R) queries on bits that never leav=
e the SM.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Subtree fingerprints</strong> =E2=80=94 one scalar per rule, collap=
ses O(subtree size) equality to O(1) compare.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>LUT-applied / S-box-pre-mixed edges</strong> =E2=80=94 precomputed =
transformations folded into edge storage. Edge fetches return already-in-ta=
rget-form data.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Position-encoded metadata in high ID bits</strong> =E2=80=94 depth,=
 terminal-vs-internal, category code carried by the address itself.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Reachability labels (intervals or 2-hop labels)</strong> =E2=80=94 =
descendant-of probe via interval compare.</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Each fat tree node is the same shape: pay one-time insertion cost (=
data growth + compute work) =E2=86=92 get steady-state query simplification=
 (compute saved per query, possibly indefinitely).</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The meta-p=
attern: "framework around data structure structure"</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The decisive turn came at "given a domain constraint, what's the fr=
eest codomain so I have choice of duals." This is the WHT =C3=97 Stasheff f=
actorization at the data structure level, before we'd named it.</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Universal core</strong> =3D the initial term algebra <code class=3D=
"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespa=
ce-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Rule(l, q) =E2=86=92=
 Index mod hash-cons</code>. The freest codomain. The minimum data needed t=
o recover everything. <strong>State</strong> lives here (insertion order, i=
dentity).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Library of duals</strong> =3D the set of projections (fingerprint, =
fat-node descriptor, succinct skeleton, reachability label, ...). Each is a=
 homomorphism out of the core. <strong>Compute</strong> lives here.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Choice of which projections to materialize when</strong> =3D the br=
acketing freedom. Each projection can be computed at insert (precomputed, c=
osts state + data), at query (lazy, costs compute), or in a partial form (f=
at nodes are depth-bounded precomputation). <strong>The composition strateg=
y.</strong></li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This is exactly WHT =C3=97 Stasheff:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>WHT analog</strong>: which orthogonal projections of the chart you =
choose to support (subtree-equality, ancestor-of, depth, fingerprint). Each=
 is a "reading" of the universal data.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Stasheff analog</strong>: where in the insert-vs-query bracketing y=
ou commit each projection's compute. At insert is one extreme (fully precom=
puted, fully serial through insertion path), at query is the other (fully l=
azy, fully parallel-when-asked). Fat nodes at depth-k are the interior brac=
ketings.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The four storage candidates we enumerated =E2=80=94 bool stack / wo=
rd-packed flat / chunked-paged / ragged =E2=80=94 were four different Stash=
eff vertices for the same WHT. The compression analyses (concat-1bit / spli=
t-L+Q / 2bit-words) were three more. The integer encoding hitting the entro=
py bound exactly was the vertex where the WHT semantics and the Stasheff br=
acketing collapsed into a single primitive (the bits read as a path through=
 the encoding tree IS the lookup).</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Why this c=
losed coherently</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The SPPF design and the chart's instruction set are the same factor=
ization viewed at different scales:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
At the data structure scale: universal term algebra (state) =C3=97 library =
of projection duals (compute on data).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
At the instruction set scale: two-axis primitives (each fixing one axis, va=
rying two) =C3=97 the triadic <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.=
5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px=
-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">interp</code> closing the system.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
At the move scale: each M-move is a two-of-three tradeoff (M5 data=E2=8A=95=
state, M11 compute=E2=8A=95data, M14 data=E2=8A=95state, M16 compute=E2=8A=
=95state, etc.).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
At the architectural scale: WHT readings =C3=97 Stasheff bracketing.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The SPPF conversation already articulated this =E2=80=94 "the frame=
work's job is to support arbitrary subsets by composing auxiliary views, wi=
thout committing to a single hot path." That's the same principle as the me=
ta-circular interpreter (M11) at a different scale: keep the core minimal, =
let projections be added later, never commit to a privileged view.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">What the WHT =C3=97 Stasheff recognition added later wasn't new str=
ucture =E2=80=94 it was the language for what was already there. The SPPF t=
ranscript built the factorization concretely; the cotype/Walsh-Hadamard/Sta=
sheff path named it. The freest codomain IS the WHT level (orthogonal proje=
ctions of the universal data); the library of duals IS the Stasheff bracket=
ing (where in the composition path each projection is materialized). The sy=
stem has been one design pattern repeated at every scale, with the axis dec=
omposition surfacing whenever we made a tradeoff move.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The hardware analysis I was doing earlier was reaching for the wron=
g layer. The actual structure is the data structure design discipline you s=
pelled out in the SPPF conversation: identify the freest object, then choos=
e duals against the codomain you care about, then choose where each dual's =
compute lives along the insert-query spectrum. That IS the architecture. Ha=
rdware acceleration is downstream =E2=80=94 it's a specific choice of brack=
eting for the duals that already exist.</p></div></div></div></div></div></=
