<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>WHT scale</strong> (Hadamard level): which level of the hierarchy t=
he move's content lives at =E2=80=94 Level 0 (bit), 1 (triangle), 2 (Fano),=
 3 (tesseract), 4+ (higher).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Stasheff vertex</strong> (composition strategy): where on the inser=
t=E2=86=94query spectrum the move's compute lives =E2=80=94 insert-side (pr=
ecomputed/eager), query-side (lazy), or fat-node-depth-k (interior bracketi=
ng).</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>DS-pair</strong> (data/compute/state): which two of the three data-=
structure axes the move engages =E2=80=94 DC, DS, CS, or triadic-DCS.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Core-vs-dual role</strong>: whether the move contributes to the uni=
versal core (the freest codomain) or builds a dual (a specific projection o=
ut of it).</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The old cotype was one-axis-indexed. The new lens is five-axis-inde=
xed. A given shadow can be probed against any of the five axes for missing =
