<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The meta-protocol exposes what's already true. It doesn't make V=E2=
=82=84 symmetry hold =E2=80=94 it just makes it observable. With the matrix=
 in hand, we can already say:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
For each (op, swap), the answer is one of {TWIN, BUILD, BARRED, SELF}</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
BUILD entries give concrete construction targets</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
BARRED entries identify axis-asymmetry hotspots</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The constr=
uctible roadmap</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The 50 BUILD entries deduplicate to roughly 30 unique target profil=
es. If we built all of them, V=E2=82=84 symmetry would be 87% realized (87%=
 =3D (3+50+2)/63). The remaining 13% requires either:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(R1) Enrich D with mutation</strong> =E2=80=94 but D is has=
h-consed for hash-consing's sake (M5 memoization). Mutating D would break t=
he cocycle invariance from M8. So this likely isn't the right move.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(R2) Enrich S with mutation</strong> =E2=80=94 the history =
log is append-only by design. Allowing mutation of past history breaks obse=
rvability/replayability. Also likely the wrong move.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(R3) Restrict V=E2=82=84 symmetry to capability-safe rotati=
ons</strong> =E2=80=94 accept that D and S are asymmetric to C and W on pur=
pose, and V=E2=82=84 symmetry doesn't fully hold. Document this and move on=
.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(R4) Reinterpret M for D and S</strong> =E2=80=94 treat "M =
on D" as "create new immutable cell that shadows the old" (functional updat=
e), and "M on S" as "append marker indicating retroactive change". This mak=
es V=E2=82=84 rotations meaningful in a generalized sense.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">R3 is the honest path; R4 is the interesting one if we want full V=
=E2=82=84 symmetry.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">My recomme=
ndation</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Before implementing the meta-protocol, decide one structural questi=
on: <strong>do we want V=E2=82=84 symmetry to be a fundamental architectura=
l law, or an emergent pattern that holds for some operations and not others=
?</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
If <strong>fundamental law</strong>: pursue R4 (reinterpret M for immutable=
 axes) and refactor toward axis-capability symmetry. The meta-protocol then=
 enforces this.</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
If <strong>emergent pattern</strong>: keep capabilities asymmetric, build t=
he 50 constructible complements, accept the 13% barred as architectural tru=
th. The meta-protocol exposes the pattern where it holds and acknowledges w=
here it doesn't.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The matrix supports either choice cleanly. Once we know which, the =
meta-protocol implementation is straightforward =E2=80=94 it's just runtime=
 exposure of the data the matrix already contains.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Want me to save the analysis to the cotype, or wait until we've dec=
ided which path?</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><=
