<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The richer=
 symmetry that emerges</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">What was happening under (held, enabled) was that we were describin=
g operations in a basis that <strong>obscured both directionality and chira=
lity</strong>. The directed witnessed framework makes both manifest:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Pairing</strong> =3D which two axes interact (=CE=B1, =CE=B2, or =
=CE=B3 =E2=80=94 the V_4 / S_3 structure)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Direction</strong> =3D which axis is consumed vs produced (the D_4 =
in the dihedral structure)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Witness</strong> =3D which axis from the opposite pair validates (t=
he Z_2 =E2=8A=82 opposite pair)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>Chirality</strong> =3D the parity of the resulting permutation (eve=
n or odd, A_4 vs S_4 \ A_4)</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">These four components decompose the S_4 action completely:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
|Pairings| =C3=97 |Pair-direction in pairing| =C3=97 |Witness in opposite| =
=C3=97 |Chirality-fix| =3D 3 =C3=97 4 =C3=97 2 =C3=97 1 =3D 24 =E2=9C=93</l=
i>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This is more refined than the V_4 analysis we had. V_4 was the "pre=
serve a pairing" symmetry; the full picture is <strong>how S_4 acts on dire=
cted witnessed flags</strong>.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Where this=
 lands us</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Three concrete things follow:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>1. The cotype's (held, enabled) classification is too coars=
e.</strong> It conflates witness with held-axis, drops direction entirely, =
