<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What M36 s=
ettles about M33</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">M33 found that V_4-twin claims didn't hold at the implementation le=
vel =E2=80=94 operations' engagement profiles didn't actually swap under V_=
4 due to axis-capability asymmetry (D and S can't mutate; C and W can).</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">M36 resolves this <strong>differently from how M33 implied</strong>=
. Rather than forcing existing ops to be V_4-symmetric (which would require=
 axis-symmetric infrastructure), we build the V_4-twins as <strong>separate=
 concrete operations</strong>. Each V_4-orbit now has 4 distinct working op=
erations rather than 1 op claimed to have 3 twins.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The honest accounting (recorded in the M36 cotype entry): some V_4-=
rotations carry ambient C engagement because witness checks use cons + norm=
alize. This is an axis-capability fact about the chart, not a flaw in the w=
itnessed-pair framework. The framework declares structural roles; implement=
ations honor those roles structurally but engage C wherever predicates eval=
uate. The test for <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bo=
rder-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px te=
xt-[0.9rem]">compute_to_state_via_data</code> was updated to check the oper=
ation's <em>own</em> state-write rather than exact history growth =E2=80=94=
 this distinction (structural engagement vs. ambient engagement) is the res=
idual M33 finding, now properly documented.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Where this=
 lands</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The 5-move arc M32 =E2=86=92 M33 =E2=86=92 M34 =E2=86=92 M35 =E2=86=
=92 M36 traces a complete structural completion:</p>
<ul class=3D"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:l=
ast-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-co=
l gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M32</strong>: V=E2=82=84-twin implementation (claimed symmetry)</li=
>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M33</strong>: audit found the symmetry incomplete at engagement lev=
el</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M34</strong>: reformulation in directed witnessed-pair basis with c=
hirality as parity bit; the asymmetry resolves to "different chiralities ar=
e different operations, not broken twins"</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M35</strong>: inverse-pair completion via Z_2 path (12 ops)</li>
<li class=3D"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">=
<strong>M36</strong>: V_4-extension via V_4 path (24 ops, full S_4 orbit)</=
li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The architecture has reached <strong>structural saturation</strong>=
 at the 3-axis-engagement level. Every (source, sink, witness) flag in the =
tetrahedral geometry has a concrete operation. The hierarchical RM/Hamming =
structure (M22 axis-level + M34 operations-level) is now realized through a=
nd through.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Forward pa=
ths remaining</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The structural completion opens these non-structural directions:</p=
>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(A) Apply the chart to a real grammar problem</strong> =E2=
=80=94 the originally-stated goal. The architectural framework is substanti=
ally complete; using it for free self-extending grammar / ISA chart is unbl=
ocked. This would test whether the framework actually serves its intended p=
urpose.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(B) Higher-order patterns (4-axis cells)</strong> =E2=80=94=
 the 4 quadradic cells (held + 3 enabled =3D all axes engaged) form another=
 set of structural patterns. M11 interp and M32 workspace_driven_state are =
in this regime. Building the full quadradic family would be an even higher-=
dimensional completion.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(C) Two-scale parity unification</strong> =E2=80=94 the axi=
s-level WHT parity (M22) and operations-level chirality (M34) are the same =
Hamming parity bit at different scales. A unified Hamming-coded address spa=
ce for the entire architecture is structurally implied but not built. This =
would crystallize the multi-scale Reed-Muller structure into a single codin=
g scheme.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(D) Apply the engagement audit to all 24 ops</strong> =E2=
=80=94 re-run M33's instrumentation against the now-populated 24-op set. Qu=
antify how many ops have "clean" engagement profiles vs. how many carry amb=
ient C engagement. This would give an honest map of where axis-capability a=
symmetry remains.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Direction (A) is the original goal =E2=80=94 the framework was buil=
t for it. Direction (D) is structural housekeeping that would close the M33=
 thread definitively. (B) and (C) are deeper structural completions that ma=
y not be necessary.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Direction's yours.</p></div></div><div class=3D"flex flex-col gap-2=
