-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">What M39 settles</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">Your synthesis names what the prior moves were realizing without na=
ming. The architecture isn't computing arbitrary functions on F_2^n =E2=80=
=94 it's selecting the canonical <strong>2^n Walsh=E2=80=93Hadamard charact=
ers</strong> as a structured basis and organizing them into a symmetry-gove=
rned algebra. The witness axis isn't just a label; it's a character index. =
The codeword width 2n + 1 is exactly the dimensions needed to address (basi=
s =C3=97 parity =C3=97 pairing).</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The two non-trivial facts that fall out:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>The 4-axis structure isn't an accident of "we chose 4 thing=
s to track."</strong> F_2^2 has 4 elements; there are 4 WHT characters =CF=
=87_00, =CF=87_01, =CF=87_10, =CF=87_11. The architecture's level is determ=
ined by the data width n, and there are precisely 2^n basis transforms at t=
hat level. The "4 axes (D, C, S, W)" labeling we've been using corresponds =
1-1 with the 4 characters =E2=80=94 D =3D =CF=87_00 is the constant DC char=
acter, the others are non-trivial parity probes.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Cayley-Dickson is a structural scaling, not a numerical dou=
bling.</strong> Each level adds 1 bit to the data width n, doubles the basi=
s to 2^(n+1) characters, extends pairing and witness bits by 1 each, and pr=
eserves chirality. The codeword scaling 5 bits (level 2) =E2=86=92 7 bits (=
level 3, Hamming(7,4)) =E2=86=92 9 bits (level 4) =E2=86=92 2n+1 bits (leve=
l n) is the level structure of the ladder.</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">The princi=
ple, restated for the cotype</h3>
<blockquote class=3D"ml-2 border-l-4 border-border-300/10 pl-4 text-text-30=
0">
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>At level n, the architecture realizes the 2^n Walsh=E2=80=
=93Hadamard basis transforms of F_2^n, organized in a (2n+1)-bit codeword s=
pace with parity-coded group symmetries V_4 / Z_3 / Z_2. Each operation ind=
exes a basis character (via its witness axis), carries a parity tag (chiral=
ity), sits in a pairing structure (Z_3 routing), and composes under control=
led symmetries. The level-n =E2=86=92 level-(n+1) scaling is a Cayley=E2=80=
=93Dickson-like ladder preserving this structure.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">This is now the test for any future move: does it respect the parit=
y-coded Hadamard-basis framing?</p>
<h3 class=3D"text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold">Where this=
 lands us</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The framework is no longer a collection of structural facts =E2=80=
=94 it's a single principle with verified implementation. 166 tests still p=
ass; the new hadamard_basis.py adds explicit WHT character computation at a=
ny level with orthogonality and completeness verified at levels 2 and 3.</p=
>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The forward directions from M38 are now sharper:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(A)</strong> Apply the chart to a real grammar problem =E2=
=80=94 the principle "computation =3D parity-basis mixing" gives a clean in=
terpretive lens for what the chart actually does on inputs.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(D)</strong> Engagement audit at 24-op level =E2=80=94 now =
reads as "does each operation cleanly engage one WHT character via its witn=
ess?"</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>(E)</strong> Higher Hadamard levels =E2=80=94 now templated=
 AND principled. Level 3 =3D 7-bit codewords addressing 8 WHT characters; l=
evel 4 =3D 9 bits and 16 characters; etc. The principle constrains what's v=
alid at each level.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The cotype is now in a state where M30=E2=86=92M39 traces a complet=
e arc: from "claimed V_4 symmetry didn't hold" through "directed witnessed =
pairs + chirality" through "Z_2 and V_4 and Z_3 generators" through "unifie=
d Hamming codeword" to "principle: parity-basis mixing." The architecture's=
 substrate is now named.</p>
