ncretely</h3>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The grammar is already in <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border borde=
r-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem=
] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">chart.py</code> =E2=80=94 <code class=3D"bg-tex=
t-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-=
wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">default_table</code> has be=
en the SKI rules as cons-cell data since M11. What's new is <strong>using i=
t through the lens of everything we built afterward</strong>. Six demonstra=
tions:</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>The grammar is its own data.</strong> <code class=3D"bg-tex=
t-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-=
wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">default_table</code> decode=
d shows three rules =E2=80=94 I-rule, K-rule, S-rule =E2=80=94 each a (patt=
ern, replacement) cons-cell, the table itself a NIL-terminated list. No hid=
den machinery: rules are first-class terms.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>apply =E2=89=A1 interp at matched granularity.</strong> Onc=
e compared one-step-to-one-step and full-to-full, the hardcoded <code class=
=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 white=
space-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">apply</code> and =
data-driven <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-30=
0 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9=
rem]">interp(default_table, _)</code> agree on all four test expressions. T=
he hardcoded path optimizes; the data-driven path expresses. They compute t=
he same function.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Hash-consing realizes SPPF.</strong> <code class=3D"bg-text=
-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-w=
rap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">cons(I, TRUE)</code> called =
twice returns the same cell ID (26). <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bo=
rder-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4=
rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">cons(cons(S, K), I)</code> built via differe=
nt construction paths produces the same cell (33), sharing the intermediate=
 <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dang=
er-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">cons(=
S, K)</code> (cell 29). The chart's <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bor=
der-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4r=
em] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">_hashcons</code> is the SPPF backing store; 3=
3 distinct pairs back 34 cells.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>A program covering 8 different orbits.</strong> The 8-step =
program threads apply =E2=86=92 store =E2=86=92 evolve_with_receipt =E2=86=
=92 validated_store =E2=86=92 quote_via_state =E2=86=92 load_with_log =E2=
=86=92 workspace_witness =E2=86=92 interp. Each step has a distinct unified=
 codeword spanning multiple chiralities, pairings, and witnesses =E2=80=94 =
a genuine tour through the 24-op vocabulary.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Spectral signature is operationally informative.</strong> P=
rojecting the 8-step trace to 3 bits (chirality + witness) gives signal vec=
tor <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-d=
anger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">[0=
, 1, 2, 1, 0, 1, 2, 1]</code>. The WHT gives <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 b=
order border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap roun=
ded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">[+8, 0, -4, -4, 0, 0, 0, 0]</code> =
=E2=80=94 the DC component is total op count, and the program's specific si=
gnature is F[2] =3D F[3] =3D -4. Different programs will have different sig=
natures; this is real analysis, not decoration.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]"><strong>Self-evaluation is non-trivially fruitful.</strong> <code c=
lass=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 w=
hitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">interp(defaul=
t_table, default_table)</code> is NOT a fixed point. The table contains the=
 I-pattern <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300=
 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9r=
em]">(I v1)</code> as data; interp recurses, finds it, matches it against t=
he I-rule (variable matches variable), and the rule fires. After one iterat=
ion, the table reaches a fixed point under further interp. The grammar appl=
ied to itself reduces meaningfully and converges. This is metacircularity e=
xercised, not just stated.</p>
