Verification depends on the current registry of <code class=3D"bg-text-200/=
5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap r=
ounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">c</code>, not necessarily the reg=
istry that existed when the receipt was emitted. If the registry evolves, o=
ld receipts may become unverifiable or, worse, verify against a different o=
peration with the same name/address discipline.
So receipts probably need either:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python
registry_digest
</code>
or:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python
