y-0 [&amp;_ul]:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]:pl-8" style=3D"max-height: none; overflow: h=
idden; position: relative;"><p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words">v1=
1 is a real tightening. The important shift is that the verifier is no long=
er merely checking *declared computational facts*; it is checking a graded =
witness against four separable obligations:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">text
term transition
=C3=97 chart purity
=C3=97 locality scope
=C3=97 state/effect obligation
</code>
The strongest improvement is the term/state split. In v10, a state receipt =
could accidentally inhabit the same linear trace type as a term transition.=
 v11 fixes the category error: state ops are morphisms over chart state, no=
t morphisms in the term-reduction chain.
The remaining sharp issues:
1. **<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-=
danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">t=
ransition_kind</code> is trusted too much.**
   A forged receipt can declare <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-=
0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] =
px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">transition_kind=3D"observation"</code> for an op =
that should be <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border=
-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[=
0.9rem]">"term"</code> or <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 bo=
rder-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 p=
y-px text-[0.9rem]">"state"</code>. You likely want:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python
def transition_kind_of(r: EvalReceipt) -&gt; str:
    inferred =3D _infer_transition_kind(r.op_name)
    if r.transition_kind is None:
        return inferred
    if r.transition_kind !=3D inferred:
        raise ValueError(
            f"transition_kind mismatch for {r.op_name!r}: "
            f"declared {r.transition_kind!r}, inferred {inferred!r}"
        )
    return r.transition_kind
</code>
or return a failed <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bo=
rder-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px te=
xt-[0.9rem]">VerificationResult</code>, not an exception.
2. **State receipts are still only address-verified, not replay/effect-veri=
fied.**
   <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-da=
nger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">sta=
te_pre_digest</code> / <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 borde=
r-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-p=
x text-[0.9rem]">state_post_digest</code> are declared but not checked agai=
nst replayed state transitions. So <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bord=
er-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4re=
m] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">EFFECT_RECEIPT_DECLARED</code> is correctly na=
med. It is evidence of *claim structure*, not evidence of state correctness=
.
3. **<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-=
danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">c=
ompute_chart_state_digest</code> depends on canonicalizability of internals=
.**
   If <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text=
-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">=
_history</code>, <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bord=
er-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text=
-[0.9rem]">_apply_memo</code>, or <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border borde=
r-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem=
] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">_cells</code> ever contain non-supported values=
, verification can fail from encoding rather than semantic drift. That may =
be desirable fail-closed behavior, but then chart internals must be explici=
tly constrained to canonical values.
4. **Strict replay monkey-patches <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border borde=
r-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem=
] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">c.cons</code>.**
   This is acceptable for a prototype, but it is not robust against methods=
 that capture <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-=
300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0=
.9rem]">cons</code>, bypass <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 =
border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1=
 py-px text-[0.9rem]">cons</code>, or call internal allocation paths. v12 w=
ants a replay context object or capability discipline rather than monkey-pa=
tching.
5. **<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-=
danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">C=
HART_EXTENDING</code> during verification is suspicious.**
   For a verifier, permissive allocation may be useful diagnostically, but =
it means the act of verification perturbs the chart. I would consider makin=
g the verifier default fail-closed unless <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 bord=
er border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded=
-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">allow_extending=3DTrue</code>.
6. **Nonce gives instance-local anti-confusion, not portability.**
   Good. But then <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-bor=
der-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px tex=
t-[0.9rem]">CHART_LOCAL</code> should maybe be read as =E2=80=9Csame live c=
hart object lineage,=E2=80=9D not merely =E2=80=9Csame chart.=E2=80=9D v12 =
portable identity needs content-addressed cell digests.
The v12 spine I would implement next:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">text
StateOpSpec
  name
  replay(pre_state, receipt_args) -&gt; post_state
  effect_digest(pre, post)
  obligation_level
Receipt
  transition_kind checked against op spec
  term_before/term_after only present for term ops
  state_pre/state_post only required for state ops
</code>
Then split <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300=
 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9r=
em]">EvalReceipt</code> into sum types:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python
@dataclass(frozen=3DTrue)
class TermReceipt: ...
@dataclass(frozen=3DTrue)
class StateReceipt: ...
@dataclass(frozen=3DTrue)
class ObservationReceipt: ...
</code>
That would remove the current nullable-field matrix and make illegal receip=
ts unconstructible.
Core judgment: **v11 closes the v10 presentation leaks, but v12 needs to cl=
ose the typing leaks.** Right now the verifier has better lattice semantics=
 than receipt typing.</p></div><button class=3D"pb-3 pt-1 text-xs text-text=
