<blockquote class=3D"ml-2 border-l-4 border-border-300/10 pl-4 text-text-30=
0">
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">v11 closes the v10 presentation leaks, but v12 needs to close the t=
yping leaks. Right now the verifier has better lattice semantics than recei=
pt typing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading=
-[1.7]">The verifier's lattice semantics (Grade meet across four axes) are =
unchanged in v12 =E2=80=94 those were good in v11. What v12 changes is rece=
ipt typing: instead of a single <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-=
0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] =
px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">EvalReceipt</code> dataclass with a nullable-fiel=
d matrix and a forgeable <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 bor=
der-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py=
-px text-[0.9rem]">transition_kind</code> string, there are three sum-typed=
 dataclasses whose constructors enforce kind correctness at construction ti=
me. The verifier dispatches on type, not on a declared kind field. Illegal =
receipts are unconstructible. The lattice semantics and the receipt typing =
are now at parity.</p>
