: hidden; position: relative;"><p class=3D"whitespace-pre-wrap break-words"=
>This is strong, but M40 currently mixes **three coordinate systems** in a =
way that should be made explicit:
1. **Point/domain view**: vector <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border=
-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem]=
 px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">f[x]</code>.
2. **Spectral/Fourier view**: vector <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bo=
rder-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4=
rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">F[k] =3D Hf</code>.
3. **Operator view**: matrices acting either on <code class=3D"bg-text-200/=
5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap r=
ounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">f</code> or on <code class=3D"bg-=
text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-p=
re-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">F</code>.
The central correction:
&gt; Frequency translation <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 b=
order-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 =
py-px text-[0.9rem]">F[k] =E2=86=A6 F[k =E2=8A=95 m]</code> is not =E2=80=
=9Cjust an axis swap=E2=80=9D in the original point domain. Under inverse W=
HT, it corresponds to multiplying <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border borde=
r-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem=
] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">f[x]</code> by the character <code class=3D"bg-=
text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-p=
re-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">=CF=87_m(x)=3D(-1)^{m=C2=
=B7x}</code>.
So:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">text
spectral translation in k
=E2=89=85 pointwise sign modulation in x
</code>
Dually:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">text
point translation x =E2=86=A6 x =E2=8A=95 a
=E2=89=85 spectral sign modulation by =CF=87_a(k)
</code>
That distinction is the main load-bearing fix.
The second correction: the comment
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python
=E2=86=91 first entry is DC component (=3D sum/N)
</code>
is wrong under the current unnormalized WHT. Here:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">python
F[0] =3D sum(f)
</code>
The average is <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border=
-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[=
0.9rem]">F[0] / N</code>.
Third: <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 tex=
t-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]"=
>chirality_flip(F) =3D -F</code> is algebraically fine as a global phase in=
version, but if your architecture quotients global sign, then this operatio=
n is observationally trivial. If sign is observable, it is a real <code cla=
ss=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whi=
tespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Z=E2=82=82</cod=
e>; if not, it collapses.
Fourth: the module advertises <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.=
5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px=
-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Z=E2=82=83 chain</code> but does not implement it. =
That is the biggest architectural hole. Right now the verified structure is=
 really:
<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dange=
r-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">text
F=E2=82=82=E2=81=BF translations =C3=97 Z=E2=82=82 sign flip
</code>
At level 2, the nonzero masks <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.=
5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px=
-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">{01,10,11}</code> form the three nontrivial V=E2=82=
=84 elements, but cycling them is not native to <code class=3D"bg-text-200/=
5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap r=
ounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">F=E2=82=82=C2=B2</code> as a line=
ar translation. A true <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 borde=
r-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-p=
x text-[0.9rem]">Z=E2=82=83</code> action should be a permutation of those =
